      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "425fb687-7626-5a81-aa76-0cb6f040aaa3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wilhelm Batz\n- Products: Ilyushin Il-2, Ilyushin Il-10, Cessna 172, Polikarpov Po-2\n- Organizations: United States Army Air Forces (USAAF)\n- Places: Eastern Front, Ploieşti oil fields\n- Topics: aerial victories, aircraft production\n\nFacts:\n- Wilhelm Batz achieved 234 of his aerial victories on the Eastern Front, including at least 46 Ilyushin Il-2 aircraft.\n- Wilhelm Batz also claimed three victories over the Ploieşti oil fields against the United States Army Air Forces, including one four-engine bomber.\n- During World War II, 36,183 Ilyushin Il-2 aircraft were produced.\n- A combined total of 42,330 Ilyushin Il-2 and Ilyushin Il-10 aircraft were built.\n- The Ilyushin Il-2 is the most produced military aircraft design in aviation history.\n- The Ilyushin Il-2 is also one of the most produced piloted aircraft in history, alongside the Cessna 172 and the Polikarpov Po-2.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e25f8b79-02d8-5bd6-b078-2a9540f29697",
        "text": "Page: Wilhelm Batz. Sentence: 234 of these victories were achieved over the Eastern Front, including at least 46 Il-2 Sturmoviks, but he did claim three victories, including one four-engine bomber against the United States Army Air Forces (USAAF) over the Ploieşti oil fields.\nPage: Ilyushin Il-2. Sentence: With 36,183 units of the Il-2 produced during the war, and in combination with its successor, the Ilyushin Il-10, a total of 42,330 were built, making it the single most produced military aircraft design in aviation history, as well as one of the most produced piloted aircraft in history along with the American postwar civilian Cessna 172 and the Soviet Union's own then-contemporary Polikarpov Po-2 \"Kukuruznik\" multipurpose biplane.",
